 ## Overview
-Computes a tight, axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) for a 2D Gaussian splat based on an opacity threshold, replacing the loose circular bounding box used in original 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) to determine tile intersections [S1, unofficial][S2]. It sets itself apart by deriving the box dimensions directly from the projected covariance matrix and opacity, significantly reducing false-positive splat duplications during rasterization compared to the original method [S1, unofficial][S2].
